{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Use Spring Boot 3.x / Spring Framework 6.x (Java 17+) as the base runtime, consistent with the framework requirement.",
    "Use Maven for dependency management; exploit Maven's dependency mediation rules as the baseline strategy for U2 and complement it with a custom classpath-resolution layer where mediation alone is insufficient.",
    "Model binding selection (U1) through a Spring Cloud Stream binder auto-configuration that is conditionally activated based on classpath presence, with a documented fallback chain.",
    "Implement profile-based backend selection (U6) using Spring's @Profile mechanism; the 'local' profile will back the stream repository with an in-memory implementation; additional profile-specific strategies (e.g., JDBC, file) will follow the same Repository abstraction.",
    "Design the undeploy operation (U5) around a single Undeployer SPI shared by jobs and streams; the singlenode target provides the in-JVM implementation referenced by the linked PR.",
    "Treat the XD -> s-c-s porting foundation (U7) as a design spike plus a thin compatibility shim package; the actual module migration is out of scope for this increment.",
    "Expose counter/metrics (U8) through Spring Boot Actuator endpoints backed by Micrometer, exposing the same counter sources that feed the firehose pipe.",
    "Publish s-c-d images (U3) via a CI workflow (GitHub Actions style) triggered on tagged commits, building a multi-arch Docker image and pushing to Docker Hub under a dedicated repository.",
    "Treat the screencast (U4) as a content deliverable produced by the same developer (screen capture + light editing + upload) rather than a separate media team engagement.",
    "Assume incremental, trunk-based development on the existing spring-cloud-dataflow monorepo with existing modules (Admin, Skipper, etc.) as the integration target."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "A single experienced s-c-d developer performs all work; estimates reflect a person familiar with Spring Cloud Data Flow, Spring Cloud Stream, Spring Boot and Maven.",
    "One workday equals 8 productive hours; no allowance is included for holidays, meetings beyond normal stand-ups, or onboarding.",
    "The existing s-c-d and s-c-s codebases are available locally; setting up the dev environment is not counted as a separate activity.",
    "U2 (dependency resolution) is bounded to a runtime classpath resolution service for the local/singlenode deployer; a full distributed/remote resolution system is out of scope.",
    "U5 (undeploy) is bounded to the singlenode target; cluster-mode undeploy is explicitly out of scope for this increment.",
    "U7 (XD module porting foundation) is bounded to brainstorming and a written design plus a minimal shim skeleton; the actual porting of XD modules is out of scope.",
    "U3 (DockerHub publishing) is bounded to configuring the CI pipeline and a single repository push; multi-account or signed/distroless image hardening is not included.",
    "U4 (screencast) is treated as a development-included deliverable: 1 day is sufficient for recording ~5-10 minutes, light editing, and public hosting.",
    "Unit tests are written inline as part of each implementation activity; the 'integration testing' activity only covers cross-story end-to-end scenarios.",
    "Documentation updates are limited to README/Markdown updates for the affected modules; no full user-guide rewrite is included."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Requirements analysis and high-level design",
      "activity_description": "Read all 8 user stories, inspect the existing s-c-d/s-c-s codebase, and produce a short design note that maps each story to concrete code areas, calls out dependencies between stories (e.g., U6/U5/U8 touching the Admin app, U1/U2 touching the deployer), and sequences the work."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Investigate binding include/exclude and fallback strategy",
      "activity_description": "Investigate how Spring Cloud Stream binders and message-bus jars are currently selected on the classpath, document the selection mechanism, evaluate options for include/exclude rules, and decide on a fallback strategy when no explicit binding is configured."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Implement binding selection and fallback mechanism",
      "activity_description": "Implement the chosen include/exclude and fallback mechanism in the s-c-d deployer (Maven coordinates, conditional bean wiring, and configuration properties), wire it into the singlenode target, and add unit tests for the selection rules and fallback path."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Design dependency resolution approach",
      "activity_description": "Design the runtime dependency resolution service: how versions are declared per module, how conflicts are detected, how the 'winning' artifact set is assembled, and how it integrates with the singlenode deployer classpath."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Implement dependency resolution service",
      "activity_description": "Implement the resolution service, the conflict-detection logic, and the integration point that adds the resolved jars to the singlenode deployer's runtime classpath. Include unit tests covering the spring-data version-conflict example from the story and a few additional cases."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Add profile support to the core Admin application",
      "activity_description": "Introduce Spring @Profile annotations and the corresponding configuration metadata on the core Admin application, refactor the stream repository wiring so the active profile selects the backend implementation, and ensure the default (no-profile) behavior remains backward compatible."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Implement in-memory strategy for the 'local' profile",
      "activity_description": "Implement the in-memory StreamRepository (and any required supporting services) that backs the Admin app when the 'local' profile is active, with unit tests for CRUD and basic query operations."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Design consistent undeploy strategy for jobs and streams",
      "activity_description": "Decide on a consistent undeploy contract applicable to both jobs and streams, document the Undeployer SPI, and align the singlenode implementation with the proposed PR referenced in the story."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Implement undeploy operation for the singlenode target",
      "activity_description": "Implement the undeploy REST endpoint and the in-JVM undeployer for the singlenode target, ensuring it tears down the running app, releases the resolved classpath, and updates the repository state. Add integration tests that deploy then undeploy a sample stream."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Brainstorm and design XD-to-s-c-s module porting foundation",
      "activity_description": "Hold a design spike, document the differences between XD modules and s-c-s modules, define the compatibility shim interface, and scaffold the minimal base package that future migrated modules will extend. No actual module is migrated in this increment."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "U8 - Expose counter (metrics) endpoints",
      "activity_description": "Enable Spring Boot Actuator, register Micrometer counter sources that wrap the existing counter service, expose HTTP endpoints under /actuator/metrics and /actuator/counters, and add a small integration test that the firehose | counter pipe can be consumed from the new endpoints."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "U3 - Set up DockerHub publishing pipeline",
      "activity_description": "Add a CI workflow (e.g., GitHub Actions) that builds the s-c-d Docker image on tagged commits, authenticates to Docker Hub using repository secrets, tags the image with the version + 'latest' where appropriate, and pushes it. Validate with one end-to-end manual run."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A13",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Create public screencast of the firehose | counter pipe",
      "activity_description": "Record a short screencast (screen capture) demonstrating the firehose | counter pipe running on s-c-s, perform light editing, and publish it to a public host (e.g., YouTube) with a short description and link in the repo README."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A14",
      "activity_name": "Cross-story integration testing",
      "activity_description": "Build and run end-to-end tests that exercise the affected stories together: deploy a stream with conflicting jar versions (U1+U2), then undeploy it (U5), with metrics exposed (U8) and the 'local' profile active (U6). Capture and triage any cross-cutting issues."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A15",
      "activity_name": "Documentation updates and increment wrap-up",
      "activity_description": "Update module READMEs and any relevant reference docs to describe the new profile-based backend, the undeploy operation, the dependency resolution behavior, the metrics endpoints, and the Docker Hub image location. Final code review pass and PR merge."
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 45
  }
}
```

